{"term":"manufacture","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:b9d97780c5700399d8","definition":"The action or process of making goods systematically or on a large scale.","example":"After years of exporting the gum base to be used as an ingredient in the manufacture of regular chewing gum, the cooperative recently decided to start making its own gum using only chicle gum base and natural flavorings and sweeteners, Chicza said.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["manufact","manufactory"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/manufacture#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:19e56bb5271005d5ae","definition":"Anything made, formed or produced; product.","example":"The roads [are] crowded with carriers, laden with rich manufactures.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["manufact","manufactory"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/manufacture#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c1c47a3fc5f5ce554b","definition":"The process of such production; generation, creation.","example":"Our lawgivers take special pride in the ever active manufacture of new bills and laws.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"figuratively","wordFamily":["manufact","manufactory"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/manufacture#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:2fe85f1ae226ec2b22","definition":"A watch manufacturer that makes its own parts, rather than assembling watches from parts obtained from other firms.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"